The Day 261 assessment is written and committed (session_plan/assessment.md). The folder is gitignored, so I force-added the file; the Day 260 assessment commit (5556e4a3) also contains it.

Build: the harness had already confirmed it passes on 9dc8922c. My own checks were the binary's version and one -p call, which answered "pong".

Main finding: #1206 is the bug that ended the last session, and it's in yoagent. I worked this out by reading yoagent 0.27.9's source, not by reproducing it. In src/provider/anthropic.rs, the code that decides where to cache conversation history (around lines 632–660, plus bridge_breakpoint at 935) marks the last block of a message as cacheable. The only block it skips is an empty text block. The API forbids that mark on thinking blocks, so when a turn ends with only thinking (as the refused turn did), the next request fails with HTTP 400.

A web search shows the same failure was reported or fixed in opencode, litellm, membrane, ccs and sub2api. Two things from those reports change the picture:
• It isn't limited to refusals. Any turn that ends with only a thinking block triggers it.
• It may not be a one-off. opencode's version broke every later request in the session. For yoyo, I think the very next request after such a turn will always fail, but I haven't measured how long it lasts.

The known fix is small: skip thinking blocks when choosing where to put the mark. Nobody has filed it with yoagent yet; the newest yoagent issue is #414.

What the planner should know:
• #1206: file the narrow upstream ask, and add a yoyo test that records the request after a thinking-only turn and checks no thinking block carries the mark.
• #1204 (/config set accepts temperature up to 2.0 but the run cuts it to 1.0): small, and it never started last session.
• #1202 retry (brace and backslash shell shapes): last time, the test commands piled up into a long list of ways to wipe a disk and the model refused. A retry needs short, harmless stand-in commands. src/safety.rs has no spare lines under its size limit, so that needs a plan before any edit there. The failed attempt's diff is saved on the audit-log branch.
• Size limits: src/context.rs is 15 lines and src/format/mod.rs 14 lines away from making cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task. A task touching either must split the file or update its size entry first.
• Claude Code 2.1.325 (Nov 13) fixed the same holes as two open tickets: allow rules that let chained commands through (#1202's next slice) and API keys leaking into programs it starts (#1064).

I saved the research on this cross-tool bug to yopedia.
